    "created_at": "2026-08-26T00:39:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-26T00:39:16Z",
    "body": "> Re the \"initial state is platform-dependent\" concern: for USB CDC-ACM devices it's fully deterministic — it's just the SET_CONTROL_LINE_STATE (bmRequestType 0x21, bRequest 0x22) the host sends on open.\n\nThe important caveat here is that the browser does not have access to send USB CDC-ACM commands directly. It is dependent on the behavior of the platform's USB CDC-ACM driver.\n\nI think the feature request tracked in #141, adding a `reconfigure()` method which can change the baud rate without re-opening the port is the correct solution here.",
